### In-container Docker (Sysbox)

This project runs Claude Code's own Docker daemon **inside** the devcontainer, isolated by
the [Sysbox](https://github.com/nestybox/sysbox) runtime. Claude Code can `docker build`,
`docker run`, use Testcontainers, etc., and the container is still **unprivileged with no
host access** — Sysbox uses user namespaces instead of `--privileged`.

**Host prerequisite:** the host must have Sysbox installed and Docker configured to use the
`sysbox-runc` runtime (see the Sysbox install guide). Without it, the container will fail to
start because of `--runtime=sysbox-runc`. Sysbox requires a Linux host and does not work with
Docker Desktop. The daemon is started by `.devcontainer/docker-start.sh` on container start.
{% endif %}
