> ⚠️ This project was generated with **privileged** in-container Docker (`docker-in-docker`)
> so Claude Code can build and run its own containers. That feature makes the devcontainer
> run **`--privileged`**, which gives processes inside it access to the host's kernel and
> block devices — it **voids the host-isolation guarantee above**. Prefer the Sysbox mode if
> your host supports it; otherwise only keep this if you accept the trade-off.
>
> The daemon is started by `.devcontainer/docker-start.sh` on container start; run that
> script by hand if `docker` is not responding.
